<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9711" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">compulsor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		id. (late Lat.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a driver</i> (of
			cattle), <i><span class="en">Pall. Jun. 2, 3</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>one who asks</i>
			or <i>forces to a payment, an exacter of money</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Amm. 22, 6, 1</span></i>; Cod. Th. 8, 10,
			3 and 4; 11, 7, 15.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
